WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.372 --> 00:00:20.933
Jean Valjean zigzagged through the streets, hoping to lose anyone pursuing him.

2
00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:24.374
The moon was full, and Valjean took advantage of that.

3
00:00:25.335 --> 00:00:30.196
He glided along the dark side of every street while keeping a watchful eye on the light side.

4
00:00:31.136 --> 00:00:36.579
He didn't know where he was taking Cosette; he only knew that they must never return to the

5
00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:37.460
Gorbeau house.

6
00:00:38.601 --> 00:00:40.422
Valjean tried to reassure himself.

7
00:00:41.162 --> 00:00:43.664
Perhaps the man he had seen was not really Javert.

8
00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.526
After all, why would Javert be looking for him?

9
00:00:48.106 --> 00:00:51.528
Everyone thought that Valjean had died when he fell from the mast of the ship.

10
00:00:52.529 --> 00:00:55.931
Even Valjean had read his own obituary in the newspaper!

11
00:00:56.912 --> 00:01:03.624
Still, strange things had been happening the past few days, and he couldn't take any chances, especially now

12
00:01:03.664 --> 00:01:05.686
that his beloved Cosette was in his care.

13
00:01:06.707 --> 00:01:12.251
When a church clock chimed at midnight, Valjean and Cosette were hiding in a doorway on the edge

14
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:12.851
of a square.

15
00:01:14.132 --> 00:01:17.795
Suddenly four large men entered the square and stopped.

16
00:01:18.435 --> 00:01:20.777
They appeared unsure about where to go next.

17
00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:25.120
One man pointed in the direction directly opposite Valjean.

18
00:01:25.644 --> 00:01:30.505
But the man who seemed to be the leader turned and pointed straight at Valjean.

19
00:01:31.466 --> 00:01:37.207
Although the leader could not see Valjean and Cosette huddled in the darkness, Valjean could see his face

20
00:01:37.247 --> 00:01:37.947
in the moonlight.

21
00:01:38.568 --> 00:01:40.768
It was definitely Javert.

22
00:01:41.588 --> 00:01:47.290
While the men hesitated, Valjean gathered Cosette in his arms and slipped quietly away.

23
00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:51.631
He decided to cross the Seine River to another part of Paris.

24
00:01:52.572 --> 00:01:57.662
When he reached the other side, he turned and looked back to be sure he hadn't been followed.

25
00:01:58.562 --> 00:02:01.204
Four shadows were starting to walk across the bridge.

26
00:02:01.744 --> 00:02:06.607
Valjean headed into a maze of small streets, turning left and right and left again.

27
00:02:07.507 --> 00:02:11.349
But then he suddenly realized that he was trapped in a long cul-de-sac.

28
00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:15.371
At one end a guard stood silently.

29
00:02:15.972 --> 00:02:17.773
At the other was a high brick wall.

30
00:02:18.793 --> 00:02:23.516
Valjean was still a very strong man and he was an expert climber.

31
00:02:24.368 --> 00:02:29.651
If he had been by himself, he could easily have wedged himself into the corner between the wall

32
00:02:29.771 --> 00:02:32.873
and a tall building and climbed to the top of the wall.

33
00:02:33.893 --> 00:02:35.674
But how could he take Cosette with him?

34
00:02:36.555 --> 00:02:38.296
Valjean studied the situation.

35
00:02:39.156 --> 00:02:44.219
There was a five-foot pile of stones in the corner, perhaps left there so that beggars would not

36
00:02:44.299 --> 00:02:46.060
find it a convenient place to sleep.

37
00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.683
But once he climbed the pile, it was still 15 feet to the top of the wall.

38
00:02:52.123 --> 00:02:53.824
What he needed was a rope.

39
00:02:54.728 --> 00:03:00.230
He heard the muffled sound of marching as seven or eight soldiers approached, their bayonets glimmering in the

40
00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:04.891
moonlight. Because of that moonlight, the streetlamps had not been lit.

41
00:03:05.511 --> 00:03:08.292
Valjean realized the streetlamps held his answer.

42
00:03:09.872 --> 00:03:15.334
A long rope ran down the street connecting all the lamps; the lamplighter used this to lower the

43
00:03:15.374 --> 00:03:16.314
lamps to light them.

44
00:03:17.134 --> 00:03:20.695
Quickly Valjean ran to the nearest lamp and cut a length of rope.

45
00:03:21.135 --> 00:03:23.496
He wrapped this under Cosette's arms and tied it.

46
00:03:24.464 --> 00:03:26.165
"Stay quiet," he whispered.

47
00:03:26.686 --> 00:03:31.649
Then just to make sure she obeyed he added, "Madame Thenardier is after you."

48
00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:35.632
Cosette's eyes grew wide and she stifled a whimper.

49
00:03:36.272 --> 00:03:38.113
If only she had Catharine to comfort her.

50
00:03:39.034 --> 00:03:41.736
But she had left her beloved doll behind when they fled.

51
00:03:41.756 --> 00:03:43.877
"Put your back against the wall."

52
00:03:44.338 --> 00:03:48.680
Valjean took off his shoes, coat, and hat, and threw them over the wall.

53
00:03:49.541 --> 00:03:55.942
Then he wedged himself into the corner, took the rope in his teeth, and began to climb, pushing

54
00:03:55.982 --> 00:03:57.943
against the bricks with all his strength.

55
00:03:58.824 --> 00:04:00.986
In no time he was at the top of the wall.

56
00:04:01.566 --> 00:04:05.990
He lowered Cosette onto the roof of what looked like a shed and then to the ground.

57
00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:08.732
"Search the cul-de-sac!"

58
00:04:09.232 --> 00:04:11.274
roared Javert from the other side of the wall.

59
00:04:11.294 --> 00:04:13.395
"He must be here someplace."

60
00:04:14.216 --> 00:04:16.658
Cosette trembled and moved close to Valjean.

61
00:04:17.599 --> 00:04:22.563
After a quarter of an hour, they heard the soldiers leave, and Valjean stepped out of the shed

62
00:04:22.623 --> 00:04:23.784
to look for better shelter.

63
00:04:24.628 --> 00:04:26.429
They seemed to be in the middle of a garden.

64
00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.972
He found a large building, but all the doors and windows were locked.

65
00:04:32.013 --> 00:04:34.595
"What is this strange place in the middle of Paris?"

66
00:04:35.135 --> 00:04:35.716
he murmured.

67
00:04:36.816 --> 00:04:37.977
Cosette was sleeping.

68
00:04:38.618 --> 00:04:41.139
Suddenly Valjean heard the sound of a bell.

69
00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:44.622
He peered from the shed and saw a man limping through the garden.

70
00:04:45.402 --> 00:04:47.904
Every time the man moved, the bell sounded.

71
00:04:48.444 --> 00:04:53.248
If this stranger discovered them, the man would surely turn them over to the police.

72
00:04:54.248 --> 00:04:58.249
While Valjean was wondering what to do next, he touched Cosette's hand.

73
00:04:58.829 --> 00:05:00.470
It was as cold as ice.

74
00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:05.631
He called her name, but she didn't wake, not even when he shook her.

75
00:05:06.191 --> 00:05:07.052
His heart raced.

76
00:05:07.432 --> 00:05:08.052
Was she dead?

77
00:05:08.832 --> 00:05:11.233
He bent closer and saw that she was still breathing.

78
00:05:11.713 --> 00:05:13.373
But it was so cold outside.

79
00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:16.474
He needed to get her in front of a fire immediately.

80
00:05:17.314 --> 00:05:21.315
Valjean walked straight to the man in the garden and held out a wad of money.

81
00:05:21.335 --> 00:05:26.501
"A hundred francs for you," said Valjean, "if you'll give us lodging for the night."

82
00:05:27.481 --> 00:05:32.002
The man started, blinked several times, and then broke into a grin.

83
00:05:32.022 --> 00:05:35.423
"Oh, Mayor Madeleine, you gave me a fright!"

84
00:05:36.303 --> 00:05:38.284
Now it was Valjean's turn to be startled.

85
00:05:38.904 --> 00:05:39.784
Mayor Madeleine?

86
00:05:40.465 --> 00:05:43.045
He hadn't been called that in what seemed like an eternity.

87
00:05:43.065 --> 00:05:44.926
"How did you get in here?"

88
00:05:45.366 --> 00:05:46.186
asked the gardener.

89
00:05:46.206 --> 00:05:48.107
"Did you fall from the sky?"

90
00:05:48.127 --> 00:05:51.248
"Who are you and what is this place?"

91
00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:52.428
asked Valjean.

92
00:05:54.008 --> 00:05:56.911
"Oh, that's a good one," replied the gardener.

93
00:05:56.931 --> 00:06:01.895
"I'm Fauchelevent and this is the convent where you found me employment as a gardener."

94
00:06:01.915 --> 00:06:04.877
"But what are you doing out here so late?

95
00:06:05.418 --> 00:06:06.519
And why do you wear a bell?"

96
00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:10.642
"I'm covering some plants so they won't be damaged by the frost.

97
00:06:11.063 --> 00:06:14.285
The bell warns the nuns and the convent schoolgirls that I'm near."

98
00:06:14.305 --> 00:06:17.488
"Listen to me, Fauchelevent," Valjean pleaded.

99
00:06:17.508 --> 00:06:21.592
"I saved your life once, and now I need you to do the same for me.

100
00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:27.044
Don't tell anyone that you've seen me and don't try to find out anything more about me.

101
00:06:28.065 --> 00:06:31.148
Can you get a girl in front of a fire before she freezes to death?"

102
00:06:32.169 --> 00:06:36.052
Cosette and Valjean were soon safely inside Fauchelevent's cottage.

103
00:06:36.913 --> 00:06:41.417
It was a crime for a man to be at the convent, but Valjean also realized that it

104
00:06:41.497 --> 00:06:42.838
could be a haven for him.

105
00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:49.044
If he could get permission to stay, no one would think to look for him there.

106
00:06:49.944 --> 00:06:55.268
"I'm delighted to have a chance to repay you," said Fauchelevent when Valjean asked him about staying.

107
00:06:55.288 --> 00:07:03.114
"You could pretend to be Ultimus Fauchelevent, my brother, and Cosette could be your granddaughter.

108
00:07:03.855 --> 00:07:08.378
I could tell the head of the convent that I'm growing old and tired, and you can help

109
00:07:08.418 --> 00:07:09.179
me in the garden."

110
00:07:10.079 --> 00:07:16.064
Soon Valjean was working in the garden, and Cosette traded her mourning clothes for a school uniform.

111
00:07:17.116 --> 00:07:20.379
Valjean packed the black outfit away in a small suitcase.

112
00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:26.445
He could not bear to give up this reminder of the first days they had spent together.

113
00:07:27.426 --> 00:07:32.791
Every day, while taking a break from her studies, Cosette was allowed to visit him for an hour.

114
00:07:33.552 --> 00:07:36.735
In this way they passed several happy years together.
